comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T06:22:42.629Z","harness:claude-code","Scope extension from CodeRabbit's third pass on PR 1681: attachContextIntentReceipt's declared return type (Result & { context_intent?: PmContextIntentReceipt }) hides its omission branches. On omission it returns { output_budget_exceeded | budget_exceeded, context_intent } without any Result field, behind a cast, and isReadResultOmittedForBudget returns boolean rather than a type predicate, so a direct SDK caller cannot narrow. Typing the omission union and making the detector a type guard is a public SDK signature change (sdk-surface 'breaking: signature'), so it belongs with this item's direct-helper criterion rather than the delivered-bytes batch."
